# Window switchers (DockDoor, AltTab) list an app's accessibility windows that have a close or
# minimize button or a standard subrole, child windows too. With one page Cra showed two, the
# browser window and the empty Chrome window its page moved out of; DevTools made three, a Peek
# its page window, and a Peek parked on its tab (#242) a blank one that stayed (GitHub #401).
# Only Cra's own windows count: the browser window, a Little Window. Chromium's windows docked on
# them are groups inside them (DockedWindowAccessibility, #391).
# promise: #401
budget rss=900 stalls50=40
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "peekInEveryTab": true}
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=main
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 2
cra://debug?switcherWindows=page
expect-log switcher windows page: 1 \[main\]

# DevTools docked beside the page.
cra://action/devTools
wait 4
cra://debug?switcherWindows=devtools
expect-log switcher windows devtools: 1 \[main\]
cra://action/devTools
wait 3

# A Peek, with DevTools docked in it, then parked while another tab is on screen.
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"String(!!window.open('${PAGE}?n=peek'))","userGesture":true}
expect-log peek: from
wait 2
cra://debug?switcherWindows=peek
expect-log switcher windows peek: 1 \[main\]
cra://debug?target=little&inspectAt=40,40
wait 5
cra://debug?switcherWindows=peekDevtools
expect-log switcher windows peekDevtools: 1 \[main\]
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=other
wait 2
cra://debug?peeks=parked
expect-log Cra peeks parked: hidden \S+n=peek$
cra://debug?switcherWindows=parked
expect-log switcher windows parked: 1 \[main\]

# A Little Window is a window of its own; its page window is part of it.
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=little
wait 3
cra://debug?switcherWindows=little
expect-log switcher windows little: 2 \[(little, main|main, little)\]
reject-log fault:
